Developing an ideal text-to-SQL translation system poses a difficult challenge due to the complexity of translating diverse languages into a fixed SQL vocabulary. Conventional approaches using reinforcement learning and batch training fall short in achieving good performance, particularly in databases with high label entropy. To overcome these limitations, we introduce a novel end-to-end system focusing on translation, which incorporates an auxiliary task to capture the semantic meaning of text inputs more effectively. Specifically, we employ a column selection mask to moderate sentence structure and an auxiliary column distribution mask to enhance column selection. Experimental results demonstrate that our end-to-end system outperforms state-of-the-art approaches by a significant margin on both SPIDER and COCO-Dataset. Moreover, we analyze our model's performance using detailed evaluation metrics and gain valuable insights on database interaction. Our implementation details are publicly available on GitHub. 

